+
+Edits are applied to the raw bytes: only the matched span is rewritten, so the
+rest of the file (line endings included) is preserved byte for byte. Matching
+is done on a newline-normalized copy, which lets an ``old_string`` written with
+plain LF find multi-line CRLF text, while the replacement is written back in
